<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harold Harefoot</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1016–1040</span> · Also known as Harold I of England</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Harold Harefoot was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> from 1035 to 1040, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cnut-the-great">Cnut the Great</a> and his first wife, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aelfgifu-of-northampton">Ælfgifu of Northampton</a>. When Cnut died in 1035 his heir <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harthacnut">Harthacnut</a> was held back in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, and Harold acted first as regent and from 1037 as king. He was blamed for the blinding and death of Alfred, brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-confessor">Edward the Confessor</a>, in 1036, and died in 1040 as Harthacnut prepared to invade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harold-harefoot.jpg" alt="Harold Harefoot" width="320" height="622" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Harold_Harefoot_in_the_Cambridge_University_Library.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
